sec.p:
Task 1 (Anomaly Detection) is evaluated using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and AUROC (which measures the classifier’s ability to distinguish between classes across thresholds):
\begin{align*} \text {Accuracy} & = \frac {TP+TN}{TP+TN+FP+FN}, \\ \text {Precision} & = \frac {TP}{TP+FP}, \\ \text {Recall} & =\frac {TP}{TP+FN}, \\ \text {F1-Score} & = \frac {2TP}{2TP+FP+FN}.\end{align*}Task 2 (Capacity Estimation), formulated as a regression task, is evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Mean Squared Error (MSE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), and Normalized Root Mean Squared Error (NRMSE):
\begin{align*} \text {MAE} & = \frac {1}{N}\sum _{i=1}^{N}\bigl |y_{i}-\hat {y}_{i}\bigr |, \\ \text {MSE} & = \frac {1}{N}\sum _{i=1}^{N}\bigl (y_{i}-\hat {y}_{i}\bigr )^{2}, \\ \text {RMSE} & = \sqrt {\text {MSE}}, \\ \text {NRMSE} & =\frac {\text {RMSE}}{y_{\max }-y_{\min }}.\end{align*}
